ame tests and hooks, not the first step (none verifies sm_121 with u64 `mul_hi` on stable Rust today). Nothing from ICICLE v3+/open-icicle CUDA backends, gnark-cuda, Nocy, Snarkify ZPrize-1B (MPL-2.0) or the WebGPU entries SHALL enter the tree, and neither sppark nor ICICLE SHALL be a crate dependency. The backend SHALL fall back to the CPU path at compile time (`cuda` off), at init time (no device, driver or toolchain; `MORI_GPU=off`) and at call time (`n < 2^MORI_GPU_MIN_K` or a kernel error), each with the same bytes and the fallback recorded in the receipt (`gpu: {arch, driver, toolkit, msm_calls, ntt_calls, fallbacks, device_bytes_peak}`; `gpu: false` when never enabled). The `midnight-proofs 0.8.3` hooks patch (two `OnceLock` registries at `msm_specific` and the `EvaluationDomain` transforms, about 60 lines, inert when unregistered) SHALL live in the separate workspace `tools/gpu-prover/` with its own `Cargo.lock` and vendored patched copy (the `tools/profile/` shape); the main workspace SHALL keep the registry crate (T0 isolation check extended to the second vendored copy, RPP-007 pattern) and `mori-gpu` SHALL NOT depend on `midnight-proofs`. Device allocations count against the process cap (measured on this host: `cudaMalloc`/`cudaMallocManaged` bytes appear in RSS and `MemAvailable`, SRC-016), so a `heavy --gpu` process SHALL run under the same cgroup caps and the receipt SHALL record `device_bytes_peak`. The backend SHALL be general purpose: any `n <= SRS size`, any `log_n <= 32`, no knowledge of the program or circuit, SRS cache keyed by content (SRC-017). | Rows F23 (G0 toolchain smoke on sm_121, done 2026-11-08: nvcc kernel and a Rust `build.rs` -> nvcc -> static lib -> zero-copy kernel, 0 mismatches), A24 (G1 source compile and G2 field and curve kernels), A25 (G3 MSM), A26 (G4 NTT), A27 (G5 integration: proof bytes identical to the CPU run under a fixed RNG seed for the `entry 7;` node, a k13 leaf below `MIN_K` and the decider, stock verify, fallback, isolation), A21 (G6 node-step measurement); each phase has the gate, kill criterion and time box of `gpu.md` §6 (tasks 2.10a-2.10f); the track opens past F23 only when gate G-A records m + q >= 0.4 and the owner funds the phases. | owner decision 2026-11-08 (3); `gpu.md` §0, F1-F6, §3, §5, §6, §7; `prover.md` F5, F6; `order.md` §1 item 8, §5.5, §7 Q4; RPP-007 |

## SAS: assurance (`specs/sherlock-assurance/spec.md`)

| ID | Form | Requirement | Acceptance check | Refines / adopts |
