Status: CONSENSUS v2.1 (council vote 6/6 ACCEPT at 2026-11-07 21:29Z; text unchanged from DRAFT v2.1; amended 2026-11-08 (3) by the owner decisions in `dissent.md` "Resolved 2026-11-08", "Resolved 2026-11-08 (2)" and "Resolved 2026-11-08 (3)": speed re-plan, new order for M2-M5 from `research/sherlock-speed-replan-20261108/order.md` §4). Ordered by milestone. Each task names its requirement IDs, its predicate row(s) and its gate. A checkbox is ticked only when the named predicate passes with its declared dependency closure unchanged (SAS-002) and, for network postconditions, a committed receipt (SWF-005). Rows marked `optional: true` (since 2026-11-08 (3): the GPU rows F23, A21, A24-A27 and the tree row A22 until their gate keeps them, and A20 until G-A' fixes S) do not gate milestones (E14). Since 2026-11-08 the B rows are mandatory; since 2026-11-08 (2) they are Sherlock's synthetic-rollup qualification on FSYN data and form the synthetic-rollup gates (6.6, 7.4), outside the Sherlock C4 closure by owner decision (SWF-013); no task depends on Fenrir (SWF-014); Sherlock fee/security evidence always has its own mandatory A/U/F row (SMN-005).

Who runs what (2026-11-08 (3)): **[loop]** tasks run unattended by the work loop under their budget caps; **[lead]** tasks need a lead decision (the gates G-A, G-A', G-B, G-C, the k=19 cut, the U/F choice, time boxes, statement reviews); **[owner]** tasks need an install or a spend. Principles (`order.md` §4): measurements before optimizations; a gate between each measurement and the optimization it licenses; the soundness fixes (2.3) and the k=19 cut in one change so 2.4 keys once; S chosen before the universal leaf is keyed so 4.4 keys once; the formal design work (2.11, 2.12, 2.14) before the node constraints, the S-slot leaf and any tree node are implemented (SRC-017); tree and GPU as measured options behind their rows; no heavy run before 2.0 (F18) has landed (SRC-016).

