=20, recorded for G-A.** T1 check: `SherlockIvcRelation::new(4, 19, leaf_vk)` gives `cost_model(&r, Some(19)).k == 20` (rows 652,433; `SHK23-ivccost`). Rows 652,364 (SHKIVC05) -> 652,437 (SHKIVC06, +73 for the fixes); excess over 2^19 is 128,145 (24%). Per-gadget report (`tools/profile` `node_rows`, probe equal to the node, `SHK23-noderows2`), nr_pow2range_cols 4: own_key_and_state 18, carried_acc 2,106, prepare_self 55,788, collapse_self 239,577, prepare_leaf 26,149, accumulate 59,339, collapse_final 267,514, publish 1,946. The two collapses are 78% of the node. Candidates (`prover.md` §2): nr_pow2range_cols 3 measures 877,523 rows (+225k, worse: collapse_self 330,026, collapse_final 395,638); dropping `rule` from the leaf instance is about -100 rows (`binding` struck, SRC-001); the accumulator assignment is 2,106 rows in all. None closes 128k without an architecture change (fewer variable bases in the collapses, the unreleased gadget T6, or S and the tree carrying the target). **Done 2026-11-09** (`bbbfac0a0`, node SHKIVC06): range checks on raw prev_h, steps, h (< 2^64, 1 <= steps <= S_MAX = 16); genesis realization (a) plus a collapsed-form constraint on the carried accumulator at every height, so the circuit equals the Lean `nodeFold` (lead accepts this form 2026-11-09: it is stronger than the brief and costs about 0 rows; a literal second in-circuit collapse would cost about 240k rows). Negatives at each boundary and through the final pairing pass; `gp_fold_and_key` end to end passes (folds 64-67 s, 17.6 GB). **k stays 20**: 652,437 rows, 128,145 over 2^19; the two collapses are 78% of the node; prover.md §2 candidates close at most about 100 rows. Recorded for G-A, which owns the k outcome; S and the tree carry the target.
