21:## 2. Evidence classes and labels
22:
23:| Class | Required record (SAS-001) | Limit |
24:|---|---|---|
25:| Source inspection | path, hash, definitions, assumptions | authored behaviour, not execution |
26:| Model execution (K, Quint) | model/tool version, bounds, seed or exhaustive claim, reached actions, trace | that instance only; digests, binding, decider soundness are premises |
27:| Differential execution | oracle provenance, complete ordered observations, projection, first divergence (SAS-005) | finite correspondence |
28:| IR preprocessing / witness execution (`ProofPreimage::check`, implemented by `preprocess`, `repos/midnightntwrk/midnight-ledger/zkir/src/ir.rs:111-116`; `c6_dispatch_consumer.rs:244-285`) | baseline, mutation site, failure class, scope label "nonproving" | no constraint-rejection, cryptographic or chain claim; this is the class of every current fragment and dispatch receipt |
29:| Constraint check (keyed relation, synthesized and verified) | baseline, mutation site, reached stage, failure class (SAS-003) | no cryptographic-binding or chain claim beyond the key |
30:| Native cryptography | proof/VK/SRS/statement/backend identities, independent verification (SRC-010), invalid controls | no ledger entitlement |
31:| Target observation | chain instance (genesis, specVersion, ledger rev), manifest, call, finalized block, pre/post state, effects (SMN-004) | that target and operation only |
32:| Formal theorem | statement, premises, domain, checkable artifact | encoded definitions only |
33:
34:Every record also carries the dependency fingerprint set: HEAD, `Cargo.lock` hash, `target-pins.json` row, key manifest hashes, chain identity (SAS-002).
