wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:9:## Evidence class
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:10:
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:11:- The numbers come from raw event traces (`recursion.phase-events/1`). They are not qualified `recursion.phase-profile/1` sidecars. `decide` marks every row `arithmetic_only` (or `unresolved`) and `profile_valid: false`.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:12:- The observer is valid for the t4 and t10 "on" runs.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:13:- The observer is NOT valid for the t20 "on" run `c0-gp-r4-t20`: the RSS sampler recorded 1 failure (`sampler_valid: false`). Its rows below are marked diagnostic. The rerun `c0-gp-r5-t20` (2026-11-09) has a valid observer, and the C11-C14 rows use it.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:14:- Each "on" run has 5,973 returned-error intervals: 5,972 transcript reads (phase 19) and 1 verify interval (phase 5) that carries the expected rejection of the negative control. The in-circuit node verifier parses proof bytes that do not exist during node keygen, the genesis prove and decider synthesis; its caller handles each read error. `reduce` and `decide` count these per phase and per context (command 3,104; key_load 438; setup_pk 438; prove 179; verify 1; outside the command 1,813) and do not let them make the observer invalid. Status 0/3, status 2 in other phases, drops, timer failures, reentrancy and sampler failures stay invalidating.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:15:- Each proof partition reconciles. The unexplained part of a node proof is 0.2% to 0.5% of its wall.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:16:- The command partition does not reconcile: 18% (t4) to 26% (t20) of the command wall is outside every span. The GP harness has no caller span around `cost_model` and relation validation. This does not change the proof rows. It blocks a command-level claim.
wiki-llm/recursion-perf/profiles/c0-first-profile.md:17:- Workload: 3 stand-in leaves (k=7), 3 node steps, 1 run decider, resident node PK, official k20 SRS. Every proof verifies, the node negative control rejects, and the ledger verifier accepts the decider.
