qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:60:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:61:## 2. Does the Collapsed-Carry Constraint Make the Circuit Equal `nodeFold`?
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:62:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:63:**Answer: YES — on every witness accepted by `SherlockIvcRelation::circuit`, the combination of `AssignedAccumulator::assign(..., 1, 1, &[], &self.self_base_names(), ...)` (`ivc.rs:507-516`), `constrain_genesis_neutral` (`ivc.rs:383-400, 520`), and `constrain_collapsed_carry` (`ivc.rs:409-421, 521`) makes the circuit's accumulator fold identical to Lean's `AccAlgebra.nodeFold` (`Aggregation.lean:1248-1252`), while avoiding a second ~239,577-row in-circuit variable-base MSM (`tasks.md:40`).**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:64:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:65:### 2.1 Algebraic Proof by Cases (`notGenesis = false` and `notGenesis = true`)
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:66:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:67:In `clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean:1248-1252`, `AccAlgebra.nodeFold` is defined as:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:68:$$\text{nodeFold}(\text{notGenesis}, p, c, l) = \text{collapse}\!\left(\text{accumulate}\!\left([\text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{notGenesis}, p)),\; \text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{notGenesis}, c)),\; l]\right)\right).$$
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:69:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:70:In `crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:538, 546, 562-563`, the circuit computes:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:71:$$\text{circuitFold}(\text{notGenesis}, p, c, l) = \text{collapse}\!\left(\text{accumulate}\!\left([\text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{notGenesis}, p)),\; c,\; l]\right)\right).$$
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:72:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:73:Because the first element $\text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{notGenesis}, p))$, the third element $l$, and the outer `collapse(accumulate(...))` are identical in both expressions, `circuitFold` equals `nodeFold` on a witness $(\text{notGenesis}, p, c, l)$ if and only if the second input to `accumulate` has the exact same structural encoding:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:74:$$c = \text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{notGenesis}, c)).$$
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:75:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:76:Let us check both values of the boolean bit $\text{notGenesis} = 1 - \text{is\_genesis}$ (`ivc.rs:498-499`):
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:77:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:78:1. **Case 1: Genesis (`is_genesis = 1`, `notGenesis = false`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:79:   - By `AccAlgebra.collapse_scale_false` (`Aggregation.lean:1238`), the right-hand side is $\text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{false}, c)) = \text{trivial\_acc}$.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:80:   - In the circuit, `constrain_genesis_neutral` (`ivc.rs:383-400, 520`) enforces $1 \cdot (\text{prev\_acc\_pi}[i] - \text{neutral}[i]) = 0$ for every lane $i$ of `prev_acc_pi = verifier.as_public_input(l, &prev_acc)` (`ivc.rs:517`), where `neutral = as_public_input(&self.trivial_acc())` (`ivc.rs:518-519`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:81:   - Because `prev_acc` is assigned with fixed shape `(1, 1, &[], &self.self_base_names())` (`ivc.rs:507-516`), its public-input lanes completely determine its `lhs` point (`C::default()`), `lhs` scalar (`F::ONE`), `rhs` point (`C::default()`), `rhs` scalar (`F::ONE`), and `self_base_names` fixed-base scalars (all `F::ZERO`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:82:   - Therefore, on every witness accepted at genesis, $c = \text{trivial\_acc} = \text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{false}, c))$, so:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:83:     $$\text{circuitFold}(0, p, c, l) = \text{collapse}(\text{accumulate}([\text{trivial\_acc}, \text{trivial\_acc}, l])) = \text{nodeFold}(\text{false}, p, c, l),$$
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:84:     matching `genesis_collapse_both` (`Aggregation.lean:1260-1263`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:85:   - *Domain restriction note:* In Lean, `nodeFold false p c l` is a total function of `c` that maps even a non-neutral `c` to `collapse(accumulate([trivial, trivial, l]))` (`genesis_witness_independent`, `Aggregation.lean:1281-1285`), whereas the circuit implements `SRC-005` Realization (a) and **refuses** any witness with $c \neq \text{trivial\_acc}$ at genesis. On the domain of witnesses accepted by the circuit, the two functions are identical.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:86:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:87:2. **Case 2: Non-Genesis (`is_genesis = 0`, `notGenesis = true`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:88:   - By `AccAlgebra.scale_true` (`Aggregation.lean:1234`), the right-hand side is $\text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{true}, c)) = \text{collapse}(c)$.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:89:   - In `midnight-circuits`, `AssignedAccumulator::assign(l, bls, scalar, 1, 1, &[], &self.self_base_names(), ...)` (`ivc.rs:507-516`) assigns `c` with 1 variable base $B_{\text{lhs}}$ and 1 variable scalar $s_{\text{lhs}}$ on `lhs` (and empty `lhs` fixed-base scalars), and 1 variable base $B_{\text{rhs}}$, 1 variable scalar $s_{\text{rhs}}$, and `self_base_names` fixed-base scalars on `rhs`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:90:   - On such an accumulator, `collapse(c)` replaces each side's variable-base MSM with the single evaluated point $[s_{\text{lhs}} \cdot B_{\text{lhs}}]$ (resp. $[s_{\text{rhs}} \cdot B_{\text{rhs}}]$) and the single scalar $[1]$, leaving the `self_base_names` fixed-base scalars untouched.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:91:   - `constrain_collapsed_carry` (`ivc.rs:409-421, 521`) asserts `prev_acc_pi[P] == F::ONE` ($s_{\text{lhs}} = 1$) and `prev_acc_pi[2P + 1] == F::ONE` ($s_{\text{rhs}} = 1$), where `carry_scalar_lanes()` returns `[pts / 2, pts + 1]` (`ivc.rs:239-248`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:92:   - Because $1 \cdot B_{\text{lhs}} = B_{\text{lhs}}$ and $1 \cdot B_{\text{rhs}} = B_{\text{rhs}}$ in the curve group, $s_{\text{lhs}} = 1 \land s_{\text{rhs}} = 1$ implies $\text{collapse}(c) = c$ in both group value and exact public-input encoding.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:93:   - Therefore, on every witness accepted off genesis, $c = \text{collapse}(c) = \text{collapse}(\text{scale}(\text{true}, c))$, so:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:94:     $$\text{circuitFold}(1, p, c, l) = \text{collapse}(\text{accumulate}([\text{collapse}(p), \text{collapse}(c), l])) = \text{nodeFold}(\text{true}, p, c, l),$$
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:95:     matching `non_genesis_keeps_both` (`Aggregation.lean:1290-1294`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:96:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:97:3. **Why `constrain_collapsed_carry` is Necessary (`T7` in `ivc06_test.qnt`, `tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:420-443`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:98:   - Suppose `constrain_collapsed_carry` (`ivc.rs:521`) were omitted. Let `acc0` be a valid collapsed accumulator with non-identity base $B$ and scalar $1$, and let `carry` re-encode each side as $(\frac{1}{2} B, \text{scalar } 2)$.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:99:   - Then $\text{collapse}(\text{carry}) = (2 \cdot \frac{1}{2} B, 1) = (B, 1) = \text{acc0}$, so `nodeFold(true, p, carry, l)` hashes `(B, 1)` into the Poseidon challenge of `accumulate` and outputs the same folded accumulator as for `acc0`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:100:   - However, `circuitFold(1, p, carry, l)` passes `carry` uncollapsed into `accumulate`, hashing $(\frac{1}{2} B, 2) \neq (B, 1)$ into the Poseidon transcript challenge (`ivc.rs:540-544`), so $\text{circuitFold}(1, p, \text{carry}, l) \neq \text{nodeFold}(\text{true}, p, \text{carry}, l)$!
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:101:   - `constrain_collapsed_carry` (`ivc.rs:409-421, 521`) rejects `carry` because its scalar lanes equal $2 \neq 1$.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:102:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:103:---
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:104:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:105:## 3. Adversarial Witnesses & Counterexample Analysis
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:106:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:107:### 3.1 Adversarial Witnesses Against `SHKIVC06` (All Refused)
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:108:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:109:All five required adversarial witness classes are modeled in [`qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06.qnt`](./ivc06.qnt) and verified in [`qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06_test.qnt`](./ivc06_test.qnt):
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:110:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:111:1. **Adversarial Witness W-1 — Height Wrap (`attackHeightWrap` in `ivc06.qnt:357-382`, `adversarialHeightWrapRefusedTest` `T4` in `ivc06_test.qnt:112-160`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:112:   - **Variant W-1a (Field wrap to $h = 0$ mid-chain, `tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:456-464` `"step1 wrap h=0"`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:113:     Witness supplies `prev_h = -2` (`P - 2 = 255` in `ivc06.qnt`) and `steps = 2`, so `prev_h != 0` (`is_genesis = 0`), `1 <= steps <= S_MAX`, and `h = (prev_h + steps) mod P = 0` (which would allow the *next* step to set `is_genesis = 1` and drop the predecessor proof, cf. `unchecked_prev_wraps_to_genesis` at `Aggregation.lean:1211-1213`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:114:     *Refusal:* `std.assert_lower_than_fixed(l, prev_h, &h_bound)` (`ivc.rs:370`) rejects `prev_h = r - 2 >= 2^64` (`circuitOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:115:   - **Variant W-1b (Boundary overflow $h = 2^{64}$, `tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:445-454` `"step1 h=2^64"`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:116:     Witness supplies `prev_h = 2^64 - 1` (`HMAX - 1 = 63` in `ivc06.qnt`, passing `prev_h < 2^64`) and `steps = 1` (passing `steps - 1 < S_MAX`), yielding `h = 2^64` (`HMAX = 64`), matching `weaker_pair_insufficient` (`Aggregation.lean:1179-1181`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:117:     *Refusal:* `std.assert_lower_than_fixed(l, &h, &h_bound)` (`ivc.rs:374`) rejects `h = 2^64` (`circuitOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:118:   - **Variant W-1c (Unreduced predecessor height `prev_h = P`, `CEX-1` from `qa/gemini-quint/ivc/REPORT.md`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:119:     Witness at true step height `truePrevH = P` supplies `prevH = P`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:120:     *Refusal:* Rejected by `assertLowerThanFixed(rawPrevH, HMAX)` (`ivc06.qnt:173`, `circuitOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:121:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:122:2. **Adversarial Witness W-2 — Steps `0` and `17` (`S_MAX + 1`) (`attackSteps0And17` in `ivc06.qnt:385-395`, `adversarialSteps0And17RefusedTest` `T5` in `ivc06_test.qnt:163-178`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:123:   - Matches `ivc_node_genesis_steps_bound` (`tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:248-260`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:124:   - For `leaf_steps = 0`, `steps_m1 = std.add_constant(l, steps, -F::ONE)` (`ivc.rs:371`) evaluates to $r - 1$ (`256` in `ivc06.qnt`), which fails `std.assert_lower_than_fixed(l, &steps_m1, &BigUint::from(S_MAX))` (`ivc.rs:372`, since $r - 1 \ge 16$).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:125:   - For `leaf_steps = 17` (`S_MAX + 1`), `steps_m1` evaluates to $16$, which fails `assert_lower_than_fixed(..., 16)` (`ivc.rs:372`, since $16 \not< 16$).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:126:   - Both are refused in-circuit (`circuitOk == false`) at genesis and mid-chain.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:127:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:128:3. **Adversarial Witness W-3 — Non-Neutral Carried Accumulator at Genesis (`attackNonNeutralGenesisCarry` in `ivc06.qnt:399-428`, `adversarialNonNeutralGenesisCarryRefusedTest` `T6` in `ivc06_test.qnt:182-222`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:129:   - Matches `ivc_node_genesis_non_neutral_carry` (`tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:262-290`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:130:   - At `prev_h = 0` (`is_genesis = 1`), the witness supplies a well-formed collapsed accumulator `carry` (`lhsScalar = 1, rhsScalar = 1`) whose variable bases are the curve generator $g$ (`lhsBase = 1, rhsBase = 1`) and whose first `self_base_names` scalar is `5` (`selfScalar = 5`), including the `CEX-3` variant where `carry.defect = -r * badLeaf.defect (mod P)` attempts to cancel an invalid genesis leaf.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:131:   - *Refusal:* In-circuit, `constrain_genesis_neutral` (`ivc.rs:383-400, 520`) evaluates `d = is_genesis * (lane - neutral)` (`ivc.rs:397`), which is non-zero on the generator point lanes and the fixed-base scalar lane, failing `std.assert_zero(l, &d)` (`ivc.rs:398`, `circuitOk == false`). Off-circuit, `SherlockIvcRelation::next_acc` (`ivc.rs:282-284`) checks `w.prev.h == 0 && !self.is_neutral(&w.prev_acc)` and returns `Err(...)` (`hostOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:132:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:133:4. **Adversarial Witness W-4 — Non-Collapsed Carried Accumulator Mid-Chain (`attackNonCollapsedCarryMidChain` in `ivc06.qnt:431-438`, `adversarialNonCollapsedCarryMidChainRefusedTest` `T7` in `ivc06_test.qnt:229-251`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:134:   - Matches `"step1 non-collapsed carry"` in `ivc_node_step1_negatives` (`tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:420-443`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:135:   - At `prev_h = 2, steps = 3`, the witness takes the honest collapsed step-0 accumulator `acc0` and re-encodes each side's MSM as `(base * 2^{-1}, scalar 2)` (`reencodeCarryScalar2` in `ivc06.qnt:310-316`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:136:   - Although `collapse(carry) == acc0`, `carry` has variable-base scalars `2 != 1` at `carry_scalar_lanes()` (`ivc.rs:239-248`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:137:   - *Refusal:* In-circuit, `constrain_collapsed_carry` (`ivc.rs:409-421, 521`) fails `std.assert_equal_to_fixed(l, x, F::ONE)` on both scalar lanes (`ivc.rs:419`, `circuitOk == false`). Off-circuit, `SherlockIvcRelation::next_acc` (`ivc.rs:285-289`) checks `!self.is_collapsed_carry(&w.prev_acc)` and returns `Err(...)` (`hostOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:138:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:139:5. **Adversarial Witness W-5 — Invalid Leaf (`attackInvalidLeaf` in `ivc06.qnt:444-452`, `adversarialInvalidLeafRefusedByPairingTest` `T8` in `ivc06_test.qnt:257-291`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:140:   - Matches `ivc_node_genesis_invalid_leaf_pairing` (`tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:292-328`) and `ivc_node_step1_negatives` (`tests/ivc_node_mock.rs:358-395`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:141:   - A leaf proof generated for another post-state is presented against `leaf_inst = [binding, prog_d, prev_d, cur_d, rule, prev_h, steps]` (`ivc.rs:549`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:142:   - Because `verify_child_incircuit_with` (`ivc.rs:550-559`, `crates/mori-recursion/src/inner.rs:162-212`) performs deferred-pairing Plonk verification (`verifier.prepare` + `resolve_fixed_bases`), the node's in-circuit constraints are satisfied (`circuitOk == true`), and `leaf_acc` carries a non-zero KZG pairing defect (`rawLeafAcc.defect != 0`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:143:   - *Refusal:* By `genesis_collapse_both` (`Aggregation.lean:1260-1263`) at genesis and `non_genesis_keeps_both` (`Aggregation.lean:1290-1294`) mid-chain, the folded accumulator `next` inherits the non-zero KZG defect (`inst.acc.defect != 0`) and is **refused by the final pairing check** (`SherlockIvcRelation::check_acc` at `ivc.rs:350-356` / `RunDeciderRelation::circuit` at `run_decider.rs:276`, `deciderOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:144:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:145:---
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:146:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:147:### 3.2 Gaps Found: Circuit vs. Host Helper Divergences
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:148:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:149:No circuit-level soundness or completeness gap was found in `SherlockIvcRelation::circuit` (`crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:456-565`). However, comparing the off-circuit host methods (`next_acc` and `is_collapsed_carry` in `ivc.rs:252-300`) against the in-circuit constraints reveals **two host-level validation gaps** where the host helper accepts inputs that `SherlockIvcRelation::circuit` rejects:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:150:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:151:#### Gap H1 — `SherlockIvcRelation::next_acc` omits host-side height/step and genesis-digest checks (`crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:277-300`)
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:152:- **Location:** `crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:277-300` vs. `crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:363-376, 497-501`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:153:- **Description:** `next_acc` checks `w.prev.h == 0 && !self.is_neutral(&w.prev_acc)` (`ivc.rs:282`) and `!self.is_collapsed_carry(&w.prev_acc)` (`ivc.rs:285`), but does **not** check:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:154:  1. `1 <= w.leaf_steps && w.leaf_steps <= S_MAX` (`ivc.rs:371-372`),
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:155:  2. `w.prev.h.checked_add(w.leaf_steps).is_some()` (`h < 2^64`, `ivc.rs:373-374`), or
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:156:  3. `w.prev.h == 0 => w.prev.cur_d == w.prev.init_d` (`ivc.rs:500-501`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:157:- **Counterexample Witness (`W-H1`, reproduced in `T4`/`T5` of `ivc06_test.qnt`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:158:  Let `w` be a genesis witness with `w.prev.h = 0`, `w.prev.cur_d = w.prev.init_d`, `w.prev_acc = rel.trivial_acc()`, and `w.leaf_steps = 17` (or `w.leaf_steps = 0`, or `w.prev.h = u64::MAX, w.leaf_steps = 1`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:159:  - `rel.next_acc(None, &w)` (`ivc.rs:277-300`) succeeds (`Ok(acc)`, `hostOk == true`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:160:  - `SherlockIvcRelation::circuit` (`ivc.rs:497`) rejects `w` in `constrain_heights` (`circuitOk == false`).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:161:- **Impact:** Non-exploitable for proof soundness (the circuit enforces all three checks), but callers of `next_acc` on the host do not get an early `Err(...)` on out-of-range `leaf_steps`, `u64` height overflow, or `prev.cur_d != prev.init_d` at genesis.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:162:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:163:#### Gap H2 — `SherlockIvcRelation::is_collapsed_carry` checks flattened public-input length rather than per-side base counts (`crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:252-261`)
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:164:- **Location:** `crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:252-261` vs. `crates/mori-recursion/src/ivc.rs:426-445, 507-516`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:165:- **Description:** `is_collapsed_carry(&self, acc: &Accumulator<S>)` checks only that `as_public_input(acc).len() == as_public_input(&self.trivial_acc()).len()` and that lanes `[pts / 2, pts + 1]` equal `F::ONE`. Because `AssignedAccumulator::<S>::as_public_input` concatenates `lhs` bases, `lhs` scalars, `lhs` fixed-base scalars, `rhs` bases, `rhs` scalars, and `rhs` fixed-base scalars without length prefixes or fixed-base key names, an off-circuit `Accumulator<S>` with mismatched per-side base counts can have the same total lane count `n`.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:166:- **Counterexample Witness (`W-H2`):**
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:167:  Construct an off-circuit `Accumulator<S>` with `0` `lhs` variable bases, `2` `rhs` variable bases `[C::default(), C::default()]` with scalars `[F::ONE, F::ONE]`, `1` `lhs` fixed-base scalar equal to `F::ONE` (which lands at index `pts / 2 = 5`), and `self.self_base_names().len() - 1` `rhs` fixed-base scalars.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:168:  - Its flattened `as_public_input` vector has length `0 + 0 + 1 + 10 + 2 + (K - 1) = 12 + K = n`, with `lanes[5] == F::ONE` (the `lhs` fixed-base scalar) and `lanes[11] == F::ONE` (the first `rhs` variable-base scalar).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:169:  - `rel.is_collapsed_carry(&acc)` (`ivc.rs:252-261`) returns `true`, even though `acc` has `0` `lhs` bases and `2` `rhs` bases (`collapse(acc) != acc`)!
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:170:  - In-circuit, `AssignedAccumulator::<S>::assign(l, bls, scalar, 1, 1, &[], &self.self_base_names(), ...)` (`ivc.rs:507-516`) and `acc_from_lanes` (`ivc.rs:426-445`) enforce `lhs.bases.len() == 1`, `rhs.bases.len() == 1`, empty `lhs` fixed bases, and exact `self_base_names()` keys, so the circuit refuses it.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:171:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:172:---
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:173:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:174:## 4. Quint Verification Commands
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:175:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:176:The model [`qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06.qnt`](./ivc06.qnt) and test suite [`qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06_test.qnt`](./ivc06_test.qnt) avoid the Quint built-in identifiers `fields`, `next`, and `fold`, and are structured for direct execution by the lead:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:177:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:178:```bash
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:179:# 1. Typecheck the model and test suite
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:180:quint typecheck qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06.qnt
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:181:quint typecheck qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06_test.qnt
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:182:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:183:# 2. Run the 10 unit, adversarial-witness, nodeFold-equivalence, and mutant tests
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:184:quint test qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06_test.qnt --main ivc06_test --max-samples 100 --seed 0x2a
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:185:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:186:# 3. Run bounded invariant exploration across all honest and adversarial step actions
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:187:quint run qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/ivc06.qnt --main ivc06 --invariant allInvariants --max-steps 20 --max-samples 200 --seed 0x2a
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:188:```
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:189:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:190:## Host run (lead, 2026-11-09)
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:191:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:192:The lane could not run commands, so the lead ran Quint 0.x (inside heavy.slice) on the lane's model. One rename was needed: the built-in name `variant` became `wvariant` in both files.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:193:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:194:- `quint typecheck ivc06.qnt`: pass.
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:195:- `quint test ivc06_test.qnt`: 10 of 10 pass (honest genesis and step 1; the Lean `genesis_collapse_both`, `non_genesis_keeps_both`, `src004_height_bridge` and `lin_refines_chain` shapes; height wrap, steps 0 and 17, non-neutral genesis carry, non-collapsed mid-chain carry and invalid leaf refused; collapsed carry makes the circuit equal `nodeFold`; seeded circuit mutants caught).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:196:- `quint run ivc06.qnt --invariant allInvariants --max-samples 20000 --max-steps 12`: no violation (20,000 traces of 13 states).
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:197:
qa/gemini-quint/ivc06/REPORT.md:198:This is model evidence from an independent lane. It is an input to task 2.3, not circuit evidence.
