1:// General aggregation protocol for Sherlock recursion (task 2.11, row F20, SRC-017).
2:// Design: openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md §3.6, D13';
3:// research/sherlock-speed-replan-20261108/tree.md §4.1 (I1-I10), prover.md §6b (Q-A..Q-C).
4://
5:// Segment composition is modeled once. A segment claim is (prog, pre, post, hLo, hHi).
6:// A leaf certifies S slots, 1 <= steps <= S enabled, disabled slots the identity.
7:// A node certifies up to three slots in the order [L, leaf, R] (tree.md F8); each slot is
8:// optional, a disabled slot is the identity segment, an all-disabled node is refused.
9:// TREE=false admits only the linear node link(carried, leaf) (the degenerate tree);
10:// TREE=true also admits join (two node children) and pad (a unary node).
11://
12:// Premises (not modeled): a leaf certificate exists iff the S-step relation holds on the
13:// reference machine (cryptographic soundness); digests are injective on the carrier domain
14:// (a digest is the pair (prog, step index) of the reference trace); the in-circuit verifier,
15:// the accumulator fold and the pairing are sound. The accumulator is abstracted as the ordered
16:// list of folded certificate ids (`acc`).
17://
18:// Manifest (S3, council review 2.14, 2026-11-09): the bundle carries a structured manifest, one
19:// entry per node in children-first order with its slot bits (hasL, hasLeaf, hasR) and child
20:// references. The decider (`canDecide`) does not read the manifest: on-chain soundness rests on
21:// the pairing of the root accumulator and the statement chain only. The off-chain verifier
22:// (`verifyChain`, SRC-010 `verify_chain`) replays the manifest; the manifest hash is bound into
23:// the bundle. I9 is therefore a property of decider plus verify_chain, not of the decider alone.
24://
25:// Genesis accumulator (S1, SRC-005 realization (a), lead decision 2026-11-09): a node's carried
26:// accumulator is the witness-supplied `carry`; at genesis (no carried child) it is scaled by the
27:// bit and collapsed to the trivial encoding, so it contributes nothing to `acc`; off genesis it is
28:// the carried child's accumulator, bound by the previous proof's public input. The adversarial
29:// action `genesis_carry` supplies a foreign carry at genesis; invariant I11 (`carryOk`) checks no
30:// node folds a certificate outside its own subtree. The encoding-level argument is Lean L-D
31:// (`genesis_collapse_both`, F21).
32://
33:// Node statement (S4, lead decision 2026-11-09): the linear node (TREE = false) keeps its
34:// in-node genesis check (`genesisAtNode`); the slot node (TREE = true) leaves genesis to the
35:// decider. Lean `lin_refines_chain` (F21) maps the linear node statement to `link`.
36://
37:// Programs: PROGS = 1..L; program p runs p owner steps and halts, so one instance covers every
38:// trace length 1..L. Heights are integers below a fixed bound HMAX (SRC-004, 2^64 in the design).
39://
40:// Not covered (on purpose): the circuit relations themselves (SRC-003 leaf internals, SRC-004
41:// range gadgets, the encoding of SRC-005 genesis scaling, SRC-006 pairing), the Blake2b/Poseidon
42:// digest encodings, keygen and VK bytes, timing and memory of real proofs (measured rows), and
43:// the accumulator algebra (Lean L-D, F21). Model execution evidence covers these instances only.
44:// Record of runs: scripts/qa/check-f20.sh (typecheck, `quint test` with TREE false/true and
45:// S in {1, 2, 4, 8}, every seeded mutant caught, bounded `quint run` sweeps).
46:// Council review 2.14 (2026-11-09): 108 tests pass, 18 seeded mutants caught, including
47:// PlacementLR (S3, L/R placement, TREE only) and GenesisCarry (S1, I11); run 20261109T235258Z-F21-f20.
48:module aggregation {
49:  const TREE: bool   // join and pad admitted (D13' slot node); false = linear chain only
50:  const S: int       // keyed steps per leaf (SRC-014), S >= 1
51:  const L: int       // longest program (owner steps), L >= 1
52:
53:  // Height bound. The design bound is 2^64 (SRC-004); Quint 0.32's Rust evaluator computes in
54:  // 64-bit integers and overflows on 2^64 itself, so the model's bound is 2^62. Every property
55:  // below is stated for a fixed bound HMAX; the exact 2^64 arithmetic is Lean L5 (F21).
56:  pure val HMAX = 2^62
57:  pure val PROGS = 1.to(L)
58:
59:  type Digest = { prog: int, idx: int }
60:  type Key = LeafKey | NodeKey | DeciderKey | ForeignKey(int)
61:  type Seg = { prog: int, pre: Digest, post: Digest, hLo: int, hHi: int }
62:  type Slot = { enabled: bool, pre: Digest, post: Digest }
63:  type LeafId = { prog: int, hPre: int, steps: int }
64:  type Leaf = { id: LeafId, prog: int, pre: Digest, post: Digest, hPre: int, steps: int,
65:    slots: List[Slot], key: Key }
66:  type OptNode = NodeRef(int) | NoNode
67:  type OptLeaf = LeafRef(LeafId) | NoLeaf
68:  type CertRef = LeafC(LeafId) | NodeC(int)
69:  // One manifest entry: the node, its slot bits and its child references (S3).
70:  type ManEntry = { node: int, hasL: bool, l: OptNode, hasLeaf: bool, leaf: OptLeaf,
71:    hasR: bool, r: OptNode }
72:  type Node = { id: int, prog: int, pre: Digest, post: Digest, hLo: int, hHi: int,
73:    l: OptNode, leaf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode,
74:    cover: Set[LeafId], acc: List[CertRef], man: List[ManEntry], depth: int, key: Key }
75:  type Stmt = { prog: int, init: Digest, fin: Digest, nSteps: int, result: int }
76:  type Decision = { stmt: Stmt, root: int, manifest: List[ManEntry], key: Key }
77:  type State = {
78:    leaves: LeafId -> Leaf,   // leaf certificates (prover output; premise: unforgeable)
79:    nodes: int -> Node,       // node certificates by id (ids increase with certification)
80:    nextNode: int,
81:    decided: Set[Decision],   // decider outputs with the manifest the verifier replayed
82:    accepted: List[Stmt],     // acceptRun log of the contract
83:    refused: int,             // adversarial attempts the constraints refused
84:  }
85:  var s: State
86:
87:  // ---- reference machine (abstract): program p has p steps, digest = (p, step index)
88:  pure def nStepsOf(p: int): int = p
89:  pure def d(p: int, i: int): Digest = { prog: p, idx: i }
90:  pure def initOf(p: int): Digest = d(p, 0)
91:  pure def halted(x: Digest): bool = x.idx == nStepsOf(x.prog)
92:  pure def resultOf(p: int): int = 10 * p
93:  pure def listSet(l: List[Stmt]): Set[Stmt] = l.indices().map(i => l[i])
94:  pure def minInt(a: int, b: int): int = if (a < b) a else b
95:  pure def maxInt(a: int, b: int): int = if (a > b) a else b
96:
97:  // ---- leaf: S slots, k enabled from owner step i, the rest disabled identities
98:  pure def leafId(p: int, i: int, k: int): LeafId = { prog: p, hPre: i, steps: k }
99:  pure def mkLeaf(p: int, i: int, k: int): Leaf = {
100:    id: leafId(p, i, k), prog: p, pre: d(p, i), post: d(p, i + k), hPre: i, steps: k,
101:    slots: range(0, S).foldl([], (acc, j) => acc.append(
102:      if (j < k) { enabled: true, pre: d(p, i + j), post: d(p, i + j + 1) }
103:      else { enabled: false, pre: d(p, i + k), post: d(p, i + k) })),
104:    key: LeafKey,
105:  }
106:  // Q-A slot semantics: enabled slots form a prefix (the publishing slot is the last enabled
107:  // one), each enabled slot chains, a disabled slot is the identity and adds nothing to steps.
108:  pure def leafOk(x: Leaf): bool = and {
109:    x.slots.length() == S,
110:    x.slots.indices().forall(j => or {
111:      x.slots[j].enabled,
112:      and { x.slots[j].pre == x.slots[j].post, j + 1 == S or not(x.slots[j + 1].enabled) },
113:    }),
114:    x.slots.indices().forall(j => j + 1 == S or x.slots[j].post == x.slots[j + 1].pre),
115:    x.steps == x.slots.foldl(0, (n, sl) => if (sl.enabled) n + 1 else n),
116:    x.pre == x.slots[0].pre, x.post == x.slots[S - 1].post,
117:    x.id == leafId(x.prog, x.hPre, x.steps),
118:  }
119:  pure def segOfLeaf(x: Leaf): Seg =
120:    { prog: x.prog, pre: x.pre, post: x.post, hLo: x.hPre, hHi: x.hPre + x.steps }
121:  pure def segOfNode(n: Node): Seg =
122:    { prog: n.prog, pre: n.pre, post: n.post, hLo: n.hLo, hHi: n.hHi }
123:
124:  // ---- node constraints (tree.md F8)
125:  pure def present(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode): bool = and {
126:    match l { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.keys().contains(i) | NoNode => true },
127:    match lf { | LeafRef(x) => st.leaves.keys().contains(x) | NoLeaf => true },
128:    match r { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.keys().contains(i) | NoNode => true },
129:    not(l == NoNode and lf == NoLeaf and r == NoNode),   // at least one slot
130:  }
131:  pure def nodeSeg(st: State, o: OptNode): List[Seg] =
132:    match o { | NodeRef(i) => [segOfNode(st.nodes.get(i))] | NoNode => [] }
133:  pure def leafSeg(st: State, o: OptLeaf): List[Seg] =
134:    match o { | LeafRef(x) => [segOfLeaf(st.leaves.get(x))] | NoLeaf => [] }
135:  // The present slots in slot order; a disabled slot is the identity and is omitted.
136:  pure def slotSegs(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode): List[Seg] =
137:    nodeSeg(st, l).concat(leafSeg(st, lf)).concat(nodeSeg(st, r))
138:  // link a b defined iff a.post = b.pre, a.hHi = b.hLo, a.prog = b.prog (design §3.6)
139:  pure def linked(segs: List[Seg]): bool = segs.indices().forall(i => i == 0 or and {
140:    segs[i - 1].prog == segs[i].prog,
141:    segs[i - 1].post == segs[i].pre,
142:    segs[i - 1].hHi == segs[i].hLo,
143:  })
144:  pure def compose(segs: List[Seg]): Seg = {
145:    prog: segs[0].prog, pre: segs[0].pre, hLo: segs[0].hLo,
146:    post: segs[segs.length() - 1].post, hHi: segs[segs.length() - 1].hHi,
147:  }
148:  pure def childKeyOk(st: State, o: OptNode): bool =
149:    match o { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.get(i).key == NodeKey | NoNode => true }
150:  pure def leafKeyOk(st: State, o: OptLeaf): bool =
151:    match o { | LeafRef(x) => st.leaves.get(x).key == LeafKey | NoLeaf => true }
152:  // SRC-004 at the leaf slot: 1 <= steps <= S and h arithmetic; the slot statement is the
153:  // leaf's own statement (its slots are checked inside the leaf relation, SRC-003).
154:  pure def leafSlotOk(st: State, o: OptLeaf): bool = match o {
155:    | LeafRef(x) =>
156:      val lf = st.leaves.get(x)
157:      and { 1 <= lf.steps, lf.steps <= S, lf.hPre + lf.steps < HMAX, leafOk(lf) }
158:    | NoLeaf => true
159:  }
160:  // The linear node (TREE = false) keeps its in-node genesis check (SRC-005, Q-B): with no carried
161:  // child the leaf must start at height 0 from init, so every chain certificate is a prefix of the
162:  // run. The slot node has no genesis case; the decider checks the root (tree.md F8).
163:  pure def genesisAtNode(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf): bool = TREE or l != NoNode or
164:    (match lf { | LeafRef(x) => st.leaves.get(x).hPre == 0 and st.leaves.get(x).pre == initOf(x.prog) | NoLeaf => false })
165:  pure def canNode(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode): bool =
166:    if (not(present(st, l, lf, r))) false else
167:    val segs = slotSegs(st, l, lf, r)
168:    and {
169:      linked(segs),
170:      childKeyOk(st, l), childKeyOk(st, r), leafKeyOk(st, lf), leafSlotOk(st, lf),
171:      segs.indices().forall(i => 0 <= segs[i].hLo and segs[i].hLo <= segs[i].hHi and segs[i].hHi < HMAX),
172:      genesisAtNode(st, l, lf),
173:    }
174:  pure def coverOf(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode): Set[LeafId] = {
175:    val cl: Set[LeafId] = match l { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.get(i).cover | NoNode => Set() }
176:    val cf: Set[LeafId] = match lf { | LeafRef(x) => Set(x) | NoLeaf => Set() }
177:    val cr: Set[LeafId] = match r { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.get(i).cover | NoNode => Set() }
178:    cl.union(cf).union(cr)
179:  }
180:  // Realization (a): the carried accumulator is scaled by the slot bit and collapsed before the
181:  // fold. A present carried child binds it to the child's accumulator (previous proof's public
182:  // input); an absent one collapses any witness-supplied carry to the trivial encoding (no entry).
183:  pure def carriedAcc(st: State, l: OptNode, carry: List[CertRef]): List[CertRef] =
184:    match l { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.get(i).acc | NoNode => [] }
185:  // The accumulator abstraction: fold order is children's folds in slot order, then self.
186:  pure def accWith(st: State, l: OptNode, lf: OptLeaf, r: OptNode, self: int,
187:      carry: List[CertRef]): List[CertRef] = {
188:    val al: List[CertRef] = carriedAcc(st, l, carry)
189:    val af: List[CertRef] = match lf { | LeafRef(x) => [LeafC(x)] | NoLeaf => [] }
190:    val ar: List[CertRef] = match r { | NodeRef(i) => st.nodes.get(i).acc | NoNode => [] }
