142:### F8. Preserved properties: what SRC-001..007 become in the tree
143:
144:Node statement (segment form, replaces `[vk_N_repr, prog_d, init_d, cur_d, h, acc]`):
145:
146:```
147:[vk_N_repr, prog_d, pre_d, post_d, h_lo, h_hi, acc...]      (acc = collapsed lhs/rhs + self fixed-base scalars, unresolved)
148:witness: has_L, has_R, has_leaf (bits); child_L instance+proof+carried acc; child_R likewise;
149:         leaf [binding, prog_d, m1, m2, rules_d, h1, steps]
150:constraints:
151:  at least one of has_L, has_R, has_leaf                      (no empty node)
152:  L: has_L ? (L.prog_d = prog_d, L.pre_d = pre_d, L.h_lo = h_lo, m1 = L.post_d, h1 = L.h_hi) : (m1 = pre_d, h1 = h_lo)
153:  leaf: has_leaf ? (leaf.prog_d = prog_d, leaf.pre_d = m1, leaf.h_pre = h1, m2 = leaf.post_d, h2 = h1 + steps, 1 <= steps <= S) : (m2 = m1, h2 = h1)
154:  R: has_R ? (R.prog_d = prog_d, R.pre_d = m2, R.h_lo = h2, post_d = R.post_d, h_hi = R.h_hi) : (post_d = m2, h_hi = h2)
155:  h_lo, h_hi, steps, h1, h2 < 2^64 (assert_lower_than_fixed, pattern parent.rs:665-670)
156:  L.vk_repr = R.vk_repr = self transcript_repr (lane 0 of each child instance)
157:  acc = collapse(accumulate([scale(proof_L, has_L), scale(carried_L, has_L),
158:                             scale(proof_R, has_R), scale(carried_R, has_R),
159:                             scale(leaf_acc, has_leaf)]))
160:```
161:
162:Linkage is the associative "child post = sibling pre" with the height as an additive field,
163:Mina-style. Position is pinned: a leaf with `h_pre = 5` can only sit at height 5, so a leaf proof
164:cannot be consumed twice or out of order (the second use would need `pre = post` of a non-empty
165:step, which the digest and `steps >= 1` refuse). Ordered child coverage exactly once is therefore
166:preserved by `(digest, height)` chaining, as in the linear node.
167:
168:| Obligation | Linear node today | Slot tree |
169:|---|---|---|
170:| SRC-001 seven-lane leaf statement | consumed by the one leaf slot | unchanged; one leaf slot per node |
171:| SRC-002 `prog_d` | passthrough, pinned by the decider | every child and the leaf assert `prog_d` equality; decider pins sealed `program_d` |
172:| SRC-003 leaf-internal `rules_d`, `steps`, chain | inside the leaf | unchanged |
173:| SRC-004 range checks, `steps` in [1,S], `h = prev_h + steps` | one addition | two additions (`h1`, `h2`), all heights range-checked; decider `n_steps = h_hi` with `h_lo = 0` |
174:| SRC-005 genesis: `prev_d == init_d`, no unauthenticated carry | one genesis case, `scale_by_bit(not_genesis)` on `proof_acc`, carried acc folded unscaled (the ISSUE) | no genesis case in the node. Each disabled slot is the SRC-005 situation: realization (a) neutral-encoding constraint or (b) scale both the proof acc and the carried acc by the slot bit. The genesis check moves to the decider: `root.pre_d == init_d` and `root.h_lo == 0`. Authenticated genesis (task 4.9) is unchanged: the leaf at `h_pre = 0` binds canonical initial carriers to `init_d`. |
175:| SRC-006 decider | verifies last node under the node key as constants, pins `vk_N_repr`, folds carried acc, pairs, opens `fin_d` | same, plus two equalities (`pre_d == init_d`, `h_lo == 0`); `values = [prog_d, init_d, fin_d, n_steps = h_hi, result_be]` unchanged; ESTIMATE +~10 rows |
176:| SRC-007 `acceptRun`, replay set | unchanged | unchanged (the root `stmt` is one value) |
