232:## 2. Recommended plan: ordered tasks
233:
234:Each task names the requirement change, the predicate and the measurement that confirms or kills
235:it. T0 and T1 need no new circuit code and run before any decision.
236:
237:**T0. Row probe of the slot node (light lane, ~0.5 day).** Copy
238:`crates/mori-recursion/tests/ivc_cost.rs` (`ivc_node_rows`, modeling only, no SRS) to a probe of
239:three relations: {self, self, leaf}, {self, self}, {self, self, leaf, leaf}. Record rows and k.
240:Requirement: none yet. Predicate: a `budgets.json` row `tree-node-rows` with rows and k.
241:Kill: {self, self, leaf} > 2^20 - 5 % (k=21 doubles time and memory; stop the tree).
242:Confirm: k=20 with margin ≥ 20 %.
243:
244:**T1. Thread scaling and concurrency of the existing node (heavy.lock, ~1 day, no new code).**
245:(a) `sherlock_ivc::ivc_node_folds_three_leaves` at `RAYON_NUM_THREADS` ∈ {4, 10, 20}; record
246:wall per node step, peak RSS and average CPU (`/usr/bin/time -v`: user+sys over wall).
247:(b) Three independent genesis node proofs started together at `RAYON_NUM_THREADS=6` under one
426:## 5. Risks
427:
428:1. **Memory clause.** Without the SRC-011 aggregate amendment the tree is 1.0×. This is an owner
429:   decision, not an engineering one. A 100 GB aggregate leaves 20 GB; the task-2.1 test already
430:   showed a single process at 113 GB, so the aggregate cap must be enforced (cgroup or the
431:   `capped heavy` wrapper), not advisory.
432:2. **k=21.** If T0 shows the three-slot node over 2^20, every node costs ~2× and ~52 GB; the
433:   tree then needs P=2 at 105 GB and gains ~1.5×. Fallback: pure merge node {self, self} plus the
434:   existing linear node as a second key family (two keys, decider pins the merge key, merge
435:   verifies either key by a bit, ~4 verifier instances) is worse; prefer dropping the tree.
436:3. **Per-slot genesis hardening.** Three disabled-slot cases instead of one; each needs the (a)/(b)
437:   realization and a fresh-witness negative through the final pairing (SRC-005). A wrong scaling
438:   on the carried acc of a disabled slot is the ISSUE that `ivc.rs:318-364` already has, times
439:   three.
440:4. **Shape-dependent challenges.** The fold challenge r depends on the grouping; verifier and
441:   prover must agree on the tree. If the manifest is not committed into the bundle hash,
442:   `verify_chain` can be fed a different shape and will refuse valid bundles (liveness) or, worse,
443:   accept a bundle it did not fully check (SRC-010). The manifest must be hash-bound.
444:5. **The 95 s basis.** If the node already uses most of 20 cores, f → 3-4 and the tree's gain on
445:   this host collapses to ≤ 1.3×. T1(b) measures this for 300 s of machine time.
446:6. **Forfeits k=19.** The linear node at k=19 (if the 1.5 % trim lands) halves time and memory and
447:   allows the tree's P to double; the tree node cannot reach k=19. The two levers compete for the
448:   same rows; the tree wins only if P ≥ 3.
449:7. **Scheduler and lock discipline.** `doctorwatson heavy` is serial by design (SWF-004,
450:   `heavy.lock`). A concurrent class changes `runs.jsonl` accounting (one run with N children),
451:   `maxRssBytes` semantics (aggregate) and the stop rule. This is factory work, not circuit work,
452:   and it is on the critical path.
453:8. **Soundness theory.** Depth 9 instead of 293 is better under 2023/1646 but still "high loss"
454:   (Bünz); no formal claim (SAS-009 "not applicable").
455:9. **GPU.** No toolkit installed; nothing in this plan depends on it; a later GPU MSM shares the
456:   120 GB and so lowers P unless it also lowers per-node RSS.
457:
