1://! C6 `BHelperScalarArithmetic`: active Scalar helper in exactly the
2://! Core-selected shapes `(First, Not)` or
3://! `(Second, Add|Sub|Mul|Lt)`. Leaf and Cons/Branch are excluded:
4://! they are selected by ScalarConstruct, not by this rule.
5://!
6://! Branch denotation follows Core `plan_scalar` for
7://! `BHelperScalarArithmetic` and `pure_leaves` checked arithmetic:
8://! * `Not` reads the actual pre-helper `operandA`. A Bool operand
9://!   stages `BoolValue { !b }`; every other kind stages
10://!   `PrimError { 11 }`.
11://! * Numeric modes read the actual pre-helper `operandB`, never
12://!   `operandA`. A non-UInt operand stages `PrimError { 11 }`.
13://!   `Lt` stages `BoolValue { regA < n }`. `Add`/`Sub`/`Mul` stage
14://!   the exact mathematical UInt128 result when it lies in
15://!   `[0, 2^128)`, otherwise `PrimError { 10 }`; a field-residue
16://!   projection is never a success value.
17://! * Every applied branch stages phase `Done`.
18://!
19://! Both relevant references are read in-circuit with the complete
20://! `C6CheckedValueReadEmitter`. Reader A is gated by `enable`:
21://! `operandA` is present in every selected shape. Reader B is gated
22://! by `enable && numeric-mode`, because `operandB` is absent for
23://! `Not`; its lanes are not interpreted as a reference in that mode.
24://! The complete reader blocks, including `selected_found`,
25://! `is_data`, `marker_free_present`, raw `marker_free`, and the
26://! original Ref space/index lanes, are retained in the block. For
27://! Second numeric modes this module additionally discharges the
28://! SI22 `regA` denotation in-circuit: `operandA` must be UInt and
29://! pre `regA` must equal its reader `uint_value`.
30://!
31://! Checked multiplication uses 64-bit limbs. With
32://! `x = x0 + 2^64 x1` and `y = y0 + 2^64 y1`, each limb below
33://! `2^64`, every partial product is below `2^128` and every sum
34://! below `2^130`, far below the BLS12-381 scalar modulus, so field
35://! `Add`/`Mul` are exact integer operations. Writing
36://! `x0*y0 = c0*2^64 + r0` and
37://! `x0*y1 + x1*y0 + c0 = c1*2^64 + r1`, the full product is
38://! `r0 + r1*2^64 + (x1*y1 + c1)*2^128`; overflow is exactly
39://! `x1*y1 + c1 != 0`, retaining the complete high half before the
40://! checked projection. Addition uses a 128-bit `DivModPowerOfTwo`
41://! split of the exact sum below `2^129`; subtraction uses the
42://! 128-bit borrow and reconstructs `x - y + borrow*2^128` before
43://! the same split.
44://!
45://! Driver order mirrors Core: premises and read walks are PS
46://! (before P3), even when P3 is chosen. P3
47://! (`pre.helper_work == admission.max_helper_work`, the original
48://! separate admission bounds) is uncharged
49://! `Exhausted{HelperWork}` with all state preserved. Otherwise P4
50://! charges remaining-1/consumed+1/helper_work+1 and P7 adds exactly
51://! one helper visit; the reference cursor is unchanged. No
52://! allocation, env, frame, task, or value-slot delta exists for
53://! this rule, so there is no P6 cap refusal. The post helper is
54://! still present; there is no HelperExit result or clearing.
55://!
56://! Premises imposed here beyond the bare selector: helper kind
57://! Scalar, the exact phase/mode pairing above, staged `None`,
58://! `operandB` present iff numeric mode, `expected` absent, result
59://! `None`, task count `0`, `parent_resume` absent, origin cursor
60://! equal to the image reference cursor, and, for `Not`, `regA==0`.
61://! These are enforced, not assumed silently.
62://!
63://! Retained caller premises, not discharged here: SI08/SI21 entry
64://! coherence, namely that the helper site/mode/operands were
65://! installed by ScalarEntry from the actual control/top frame
66://! (RetUnary for `Not`, RetRight for the binary modes) and that
67://! the site lane agrees with that frame; StepInv clauses beyond
68://! the lanes enforced here; SI17 marker placement; program
69://! membership; and native issuance. No site value is guessed from
70://! the helper lanes alone.
71://!
72://! Namespace composition: this emitter owns
73://! `%{scope}.local.temp.*` plus one retained serial per composed
74://! block under `scope`. The readers are composed under the child
75://! scope `{scope}.arithread`, because both reader and parent mint
76://! `.local.temp.`-family serials; no same-scope serial is
77://! initialised twice. Caller operands under any composed prefix,
78://! parent or child, are refused. The retained emitter advances
79://! every serial across `emit` calls; the free function is
80://! single-shot per scope.
