I’m keeping the bounded VM and hardened linear node in the recommendation. The main changes are to make leaf, node and decider sizing one gate; stop treating the failed tree probe or F-at-S=1 as available throughput fallbacks; and move statement, initialization and GP verifier work before final key generation. The current manifests already show why joint sizing matters: the C6-shaped node has 741,708 rows, versus 652,437 in the stand-in profile. (`qa/sherlock/manifests/node.json:22`; `qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json:22`)

